Guidelines:
- At most {{ max_rules }} actions (create + merge). Prefer reusable preferences a review engine can match in a diff — quality over volume.
- Simple asserted org conventions are valid creates when the body is concrete (when + preferred + cue).
- Merge near-duplicates — same title theme + same guidance → ONE action. Prefer merging when multiple candidates support one preference.
- Single-PR creates are allowed when the body is concrete and reusable beyond one call site.
- skip when:
  - exact catalog coverage
  - near-duplicates of **rejected** rules, or the **same failure class** as rejected / seed anti-examples
  - clarifying questions, one-shot local chores, non-actionable hedges (“check if”, “if necessary”)
  - zero coding guidance / title-only paraphrase mush
- For merge into **pending**, supply sharper title/body when needed. Never rewrite approved/rejected wording (omit title and body or leave empty).
- `path_hint`: area-bound preferences → shallow directory glob (≤2 segments) from that area (`src/**`, `migrations/**`, `tests/**`, …). Cross-cutting → `""`. Never deep comment folders, filenames, or invented framework roots.
- `prs` from supporting candidates. Cap at 8.
- If nothing useful, return {"actions": []}.

